  Main form for rev_payment — WBS 8.3 (payment capture form). TAD:
  docs/architecture/revitalise-grant-automation-architecture.md section 9.4 (gate consequence 2,
  C-TECH-077) and section 3.1 (rev_payment attribute table). SDD:
  docs/plans/revitalise-payment-capture-plan.md FR-150, FR-151, FR-152, NFR-150. This form is
  also the artefact named directly by evidence-map rule 5 (TAD section 9.4.1) — the deliverable
  that makes the task's own outcome (a capture FORM, not navigation to an empty table) the thing
  proved.

  ALL 9 SECURED COLUMNS ON THIS TABLE ARE ON THIS FORM, SATISFYING C-TECH-077: rev_grantid,
  rev_bankaccountid, rev_providerid, rev_amount, rev_paymentdate, rev_method, rev_qboreference,
  rev_isfinalpayment, rev_paymentstatus. rev_name (unsecured — autonumber, cannot carry an
  identity, see this table's own Entity.xml header) is shown disabled, matching this solution's
  own convention for an autonumber primary name (rev_grant.rev_name, rev_review.rev_name both
  use disabled="true" on their name control).

  FR-151 (Grant, Payee bank account and Amount required before save): RequiredLevel is set at
  the ATTRIBUTE in Entity.xml (rev_grantid, rev_bankaccountid, rev_amount are all
  ApplicationRequired there already, from WBS 8.1) — this form adds no ADDITIONAL
  RequiredLevel="Required" attribute on any <control>, because the platform enforces an
  ApplicationRequired attribute on every form that surfaces it without a form-level override,
  and adding one here would be redundant with, and could drift from, the schema's own
  declaration (single source of truth for the requirement).

  FR-152 (QuickBooks reference optional at creation, editable thereafter): rev_qboreference's
  RequiredLevel is None in Entity.xml and this form's control carries no override, so it is
  populatable at creation and editable on every subsequent save — exactly what FR-152 asks for,
  with no additional form logic needed.

  SHAPE COPIED FROM Entities/rev_roundfinance/FormXml/main/{94936d70-...}.xml, per
  skills/how-to-verify-a-platform-contract.md.

  CONTROL CLASSIDS — five ground-truthed against this solution's OWN already-shipped,
  already-imported forms (grep across Entities/*/FormXml, 2026-09-09):
