    Picklist (choice)  {3EF39988-22BB-4f0b-BBBE-64B5A3748AEE}  — rev_applicant.rev_agerange
    Date Only (datetime) {5B773807-9FB2-42db-97C3-7A91EFF8ADFF} — rev_setting.rev_effectivefrom

  ONE CLASSID IS NOT GROUND-TRUTHED — marked A-PAY-1, Dev Summary section 10 OPEN, exactly the
  same open item Entities/rev_roundfinance/FormXml/main/{94936d70-...}.xml already carries as
  A-FIN-03 for its own five Decimal fields (this project's `identifier-namespace-collision-
  across-documents` class, x4, is why this feature's own dev summary mints a fresh id rather
  than reusing A-FIN-03 across two unrelated documents). No attribute anywhere in THIS
  solution's committed, already-shipped/imported forms is typed Decimal with a form yet;
  rev_roundfinance's own five Decimal fields are the only other instance and are THEMSELVES
  still open (A-FIN-03, per that file's own header). The value below,
  {C3EBB6DA-CE32-4df0-8534-30B624E393CF}, is Dataverse's documented classic "Decimal Number"
  field control id (E3 — documented but not confirmed against THIS solution's own shipped
  forms) and is used here for rev_amount. Clearing action: after this solution imports to DEV, a
  human opens this form once (the same V4 "open and save" step every new form in this solution
  needs anyway, C-TECH-053) and confirms rev_amount renders as a numeric editor, not blank or a
  text control; if wrong, the designer will have silently substituted its own correct control,
  visible on the next export+unpack.
